Description: Harden Rekordbox PDB parsing against corrupt/truncated EXPORT.PDB
 A database truncated by unplugging the USB device mid-write (cluster chain
 longer than file size) can contain page chains that cycle or run into pages
 of other tables. parseDeviceDB() switched on the *table* type while kaitai
 parses row bodies by the *page* type, so a wandering chain made the
 static_casts read the wrong row type -> garbage pointers -> SIGSEGV in
 LibraryControl::browseToggleUsb -> parseDeviceDB (observed on the XDJ400 Pi,
 systemd-coredump at 22:15:11). Fix per crate-digger guidance: only
 interpret rows when page type matches the table, null-guard row bodies, and
 terminate page-chain cycles. Verified against a corpus of 311 corrupt PDBs:
 fixes 3 reproducible segfaults and 1 infinite loop; valid files parse
 identically. (Upstream 2.5.6 parser crashes on the same corpus.)
Author: Pioneered CI <pioneered-build@localhost>
Forwarded: no

